WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.914
[MUSIC]

00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:12.126
We talk a lot about networks.

00:00:12.126 --> 00:00:16.333
Most people don't have any idea how
big their networks in fact really are.

00:00:16.333 --> 00:00:18.468
Your networks are enormous.

00:00:18.468 --> 00:00:23.040
I mean, you start with the people in the
room, you start with everybody they know.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.578
You start with people that they know.

00:00:25.578 --> 00:00:28.778
You look at graduates of Stanford,
people that they know,

00:00:28.778 --> 00:00:30.636
the places that they've worked.

00:00:30.636 --> 00:00:32.115
Before you know it,

00:00:32.115 --> 00:00:38.045
you can define your network literally as
being hundreds of thousands of people.

00:00:38.045 --> 00:00:42.699
Because anybody who can make a connection
to somebody that might be willing to help

00:00:42.699 --> 00:00:44.864
you, is in fact part of your network.

00:00:44.864 --> 00:00:49.544
And you may not even know who they are,
but they're part of your network and

00:00:49.544 --> 00:00:51.484
you can make that work for you.

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:54.748
If you want to meet somebody,
somebody, usually somebody in

00:00:54.748 --> 00:00:59.432
the Stanford Business School alumni, Kim
Marie will make that introduction for you.

00:00:59.432 --> 00:01:01.892
If you can figure out the right
way to get to him and

00:01:01.892 --> 00:01:03.696
the right way to ask that question.

00:01:03.696 --> 00:01:08.436
GSB alums will usually help.

00:01:08.436 --> 00:01:12.441
I'll make this point because
I always make it and that is,

00:01:12.441 --> 00:01:16.003
almost anybody is going to
be willing to help you.

00:01:16.003 --> 00:01:19.023
I'd be willing to help you, your
classmates would be willing to help you.

00:01:19.023 --> 00:01:22.198
Your professors and
alumni will be willing to help you, but

00:01:22.198 --> 00:01:25.638
very few of them are going to be
willing to do your homework for you.

00:01:25.638 --> 00:01:30.834
And so, an example,
if you call me and say,

00:01:30.834 --> 00:01:37.726
Tom, I want to get into,
I don't know, venture capital.

00:01:37.726 --> 00:01:41.250
Would you introduce me to
some venture capitalists?

00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:42.695
What?

00:01:42.695 --> 00:01:46.157
That's a lazy question, okay?

00:01:46.157 --> 00:01:53.163
But if you said, I've got two years
in the venture capital industry,

00:01:53.163 --> 00:01:58.032
and I'm working on a project
that Josh Greene and

00:01:58.032 --> 00:02:01.730
More David Dahl is a board member of.

00:02:01.730 --> 00:02:05.434
I know you know Josh, because I
know you work with him on a board.

00:02:05.434 --> 00:02:09.018
Would you be willing to
introduce me to Josh Greene so

00:02:09.018 --> 00:02:14.646
that I can have a conversation about this
project that I know he's interested in?

00:02:14.646 --> 00:02:16.908
Now, night and day, those two questions.

00:02:16.908 --> 00:02:21.008
The first one general,
requires work on my part.

00:02:21.008 --> 00:02:25.442
And I'm not going to go do a lot of work
to try to figure out what you could have

00:02:25.442 --> 00:02:27.058
figured out and didn't.

00:02:27.058 --> 00:02:31.679
But the second one, if I believe that
that's a very credible question,

00:02:31.679 --> 00:02:36.221
it takes me about 30 seconds to pop
off an email to Josh and say, look,

00:02:36.221 --> 00:02:38.986
this is somebody I think
you ought to meet.

00:02:38.986 --> 00:02:43.010
And they've specifically picked you out
of the hundreds or thousands of venture

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:46.041
capital people because of your
experience in this company.

00:02:46.041 --> 00:02:49.336
And they're interested in that and
they think they have something to add,

00:02:49.336 --> 00:02:51.545
would you meet with them for
15 to 20 minutes?

00:02:51.545 --> 00:02:55.229
Specific on the one hand,
general on the other hand.

00:02:55.229 --> 00:02:58.606
They said pick specific targets,
make specific requests.

00:02:58.606 --> 00:03:02.062
And then if somebody does you a favor,
particularly somebody that didn't have

00:03:02.062 --> 00:03:04.810
any reason to do it other than
they were just trying to help you.

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:08.491
After the thing is done,
you met with Joshua Hunter, go back,

00:03:08.491 --> 00:03:11.212
send them an email and
tell him what happened.

00:03:11.212 --> 00:03:13.722
Hey, I met with Josh,
thanks for setting that up.

00:03:13.722 --> 00:03:16.679
I'm not sure what's going to come out
of it, but I really appreciate it,

00:03:16.679 --> 00:03:18.373
we're going to stay in touch, thank you.

00:03:18.373 --> 00:03:21.696
Believe me, that will pay dividends later.

00:03:21.696 --> 00:03:24.715
First of all, it's just good common
courtesy if somebody did something for

00:03:24.715 --> 00:03:26.648
you that they didn't have
to do to call them up and

00:03:26.648 --> 00:03:29.498
thank them and tell them what happened
because they're probably curious.

00:03:29.498 --> 00:03:33.776
It also leaves that door open to go
back to them again in the future because

00:03:33.776 --> 00:03:36.266
they've got a good feeling about you.

00:03:36.266 --> 00:03:37.970
This is somebody that
handled that right and

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:40.422
they'd be willing to go do another
favor for you down the road.

00:03:40.422 --> 00:03:46.788
Whereas I've got a lot of people, I won't
name them, maybe I will later a few,

00:03:46.788 --> 00:03:51.443
but who seems like every couple
of years would call me up and

00:03:51.443 --> 00:03:55.646
say, Tom, it's been so
long since we've talked.

00:03:55.646 --> 00:03:59.854
I really wanted to get back to you and
see how you were doing.

00:03:59.854 --> 00:04:01.271
Well, I'm doing fine.

00:04:01.271 --> 00:04:02.873
[LAUGH] How are you doing?

00:04:02.873 --> 00:04:05.516
Well, I'm getting work out of looking for
a job.

00:04:05.516 --> 00:04:09.752
Well, what happened with the last thing
that you called me about two years ago

00:04:09.752 --> 00:04:13.086
that he never came back and
told me what happened about that?

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:15.004
And maybe I'll be polite to him,
maybe I won't.

00:04:15.004 --> 00:04:20.020
More likely they don't,
somehow I'm out of town or something when

00:04:20.020 --> 00:04:25.566
that call comes in and my EA just handles
it, it never sees the light of day.

00:04:25.566 --> 00:04:31.900
Stay connected to the people
who've helped you.

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:32.996
[MUSIC]

